screen.IRCGI=IRC Directional Probe GI
screen.IRCGI.comment=DDGI directional irradiance probes with distance visibility, without SVGF. Includes block light and sunlight only.
option.IRC_GI_STRENGTH=IRC GI Strength
option.IRC_GI_STRENGTH.comment=Scales cached indirect lighting after sky-exposure attenuation; does not scale directional SH sky lighting.
option.PROBE_HYSTERESIS=Irradiance Temporal Hysteresis
option.PROBE_HYSTERESIS.comment=Fraction of the previous frame kept per update (0.98 = only 2% of the new sample blends in). Higher = steadier but slower; raise toward 0.99 when low-frequency flicker near light sources is visible, lower it if movement trails bother you.
option.PROBE_DIST_HYSTERESIS=Distance Field Hysteresis
option.PROBE_DIST_HYSTERESIS.comment=The distance (occlusion) field describes static geometry, so it can relax slowly; raising it removes per-frame jitter of the Chebyshev visibility weight, which otherwise amplifies flicker.
option.PROBE_NORMAL_BIAS=Normal Bias (m)
option.PROBE_NORMAL_BIAS.comment=Pushes the query point into the surface along its normal to avoid numeric error and light leaks; too large sinks the sample into walls.
option.PROBE_VIEW_BIAS=View Bias (m)
option.PROBE_VIEW_BIAS.comment=Pushes the query point away from walls along the view ray, reducing false occlusion right against surfaces.
option.PROBE_IRRADIANCE_GAMMA=Irradiance Encoding Gamma
option.PROBE_IRRADIANCE_GAMMA.comment=Brightness encoding exponent before probe storage (DDGI default 5). Higher values tame dark-end quantization noise and subtly change the overall brightness response.
option.IRC_DISABLE_SUN_GI=Disable Sun Bounce (Debug)
option.IRC_DISABLE_SUN_GI.comment=When on, probes only inject block light / emissives, isolating the block-light path.
option.PROBE_ATLAS_FILTER=Probe Atlas Bilateral Filter
option.PROBE_ATLAS_FILTER.comment=Applies a 3x3 edge-preserving smooth to each probe's octahedral block after update (RTXGI-style), reducing sampling noise and low-frequency flicker near small light sources without extra rays.
option.PROBE_ATLAS_FILTER_DIST_K=Filter Distance Edge K
option.PROBE_ATLAS_FILTER_DIST_K.comment=Neighbor weight exp2(-delta^2 * K) on the distance field; larger K preserves edges and smooths less.
option.PROBE_ATLAS_FILTER_DIR_POW=Filter Direction Power
option.PROBE_ATLAS_FILTER_DIR_POW.comment=Texel direction similarity pow(dot, POW); larger keeps the filter directionally local, smaller smooths (blurs) more.
option.MOON_BRIGHTNESS_MULTIPLIER=Moon Disc Brightness
option.MOON_BRIGHTNESS_MULTIPLIER.comment=Scales the visible moon disc, independently of night lighting brightness.
screen.SSILVB=SSILVB Screen-Space GI
screen.SSILVB.comment=Screen-space voxelized global illumination: approximate GI from the screen buffer, cheap, no voxelization needed
screen.VXGI=VXGI Voxel GI
screen.VXGI.comment=Voxel global illumination: 64^3 grid + IRC cache + per-pixel diffuse tracing. Selected through GI Mode.
screen.PTGIDenoise=PTGI Denoise
screen.PTGIDenoise.comment=PTGI-style median denoise parameters (only affects VXGI; requires Denoise Scheme = PTGI in VXGI)
screen.voxel=Voxel Debug
screen.voxel.comment=Voxel GI debug visualization (diagnostics only; user switches live under Lighting -> Global Illumination -> VXGI)
