# Fog
option.VOLUMETRIC_FOG=Volumetric Fog
option.VF_CLOUD_SHADOWS=Volumetric Fog Cloud Shadows
option.VF_HEIGHT=Volumetric Fog Height
suffix.VF_HEIGHT=m
option.VF_SHAFT_RANGE=Light Shaft Range
option.VF_SHAFT_RANGE.comment=How far light shafts stay visible along the view ray, in blocks. Small = shafts only near the camera; large = they reach further; 256 = no falloff (effectively disables it, useful to compare before/after). Only the shaft contrast fades with distance - distant fog becomes plain fog rather than going black
option.VF_NIGHT_FOG_SATURATION=Night Fog Saturation
option.VF_NIGHT_FOG_SATURATION.comment=The blue of the night fog comes from two sources: the moonlight term is blue itself, and the fog's Rayleigh scattering coefficient is strongly blue (hidden during the day by the warm-white sun term). 0 = fully neutral (brightness only, i.e. grey fog at night), 1 = keep the original blue. Night only; daytime is unaffected
option.VF_RAIN_SUN_FLOOR=Rain Sun Term Floor
option.VF_RAIN_SUN_FLOOR.comment=Rain cloud shading multiplies the fog sun term by max(1 - wetness * cloudShadowStrength, 0), and cloud shadow strength defaults to 1.0, so at full rain this term reaches exactly zero - the fog loses its only strong light source and is left with dim skylight, which reads as dark and yellow. This option puts a floor under that multiplier: keep at least this much of the sun term when it rains. 0 = original behaviour (zeroed in rain, darkest), 1 = no rain attenuation at all. Clear weather is unaffected
option.VF_FOG_THICKNESS=Fog Layer Thickness
option.VF_FOG_THICKNESS.comment=Half-height of the fog layer envelope, in blocks. This decides whether blocks or the sky get occluded more: with a thin layer, looking up from inside it leaves the fog within a dozen blocks, so the sky stays clear while horizontal views of blocks stay inside the layer and get fogged; with a thick layer (256+ is close to uniform fog) occlusion depends only on distance, so the sky (256 blocks) is fogged more than nearby blocks. Thicker layers raise the overall fog amount, so lower Global Fog Density accordingly
suffix.VF_FOG_THICKNESS=blocks

option.VF_RAYLEIGH_DENSITY=Volumetric Fog Rayleigh Density
option.VF_MIE_DENSITY=Volumetric Fog Mie Density
option.VF_MIE_DENSITY_RAIN_MULT=Volumetric Fog Mie Density Rain Multiplier
option.VF_TIME_FADE=Volumetric Fog Time Fade
option.COLORED_VOLUMETRIC_FOG=Colored Volumetric Fog

option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHT=Volumetric Light (God Rays)
option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHT.comment=The beams come from the volumetric fog itself: the fog's sun term is multiplied by the shadow visibility along the view ray, so the light/dark pattern cut by leaves, windows and openings grows directly on the fog. Requires Volumetric Fog; beams share the fog's color, density and height falloff. Stained-glass tint is controlled by Colored Volumetric Fog; noise is smoothed by TAA
option.VF_VOLUME_INTENSITY=Volumetric Light Intensity
option.VF_VOLUME_INTENSITY.comment=Shadow contrast of the beams: 0 = no darkening at all (no beams), 1 = fully attenuated by shadow visibility (full contrast, higher values have no effect). For brighter beams use Volumetric Light Brightness / Volumetric Fog Mie Density
option.VF_SHAFT_BRIGHTNESS=Volumetric Light Brightness
option.VF_SHAFT_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightens only the sunlit part of the fog (leaves the ambient fog untouched), so this is the direct way to make the beams stand out: raising fog density or Mie density brightens the ambient fog as well and leaves the contrast unchanged. 1.0 = current look, 2-3 is already very visible
option.VF_VOLUME_SHADOW_SAMPLES=Volumetric Light Shadow Samples
option.VF_VOLUME_SHADOW_SAMPLES.comment=How many shadow-map samples are taken along each view ray (stratified + per-pixel dithered, noise averaged by TAA). 0 disables the beams; higher = finer, more continuous beams at linearly higher cost
option.SUN_HALO=Sun Halo (Base)
option.SUN_HALO.comment=Base glow around the sun/moon, independent of fog density (visible even without fog); drawn on sky pixels only
option.SUN_HALO_STRENGTH=Sun Halo Strength
option.SUN_HALO_STRENGTH.comment=Base halo strength (0 disables the halo)
option.SUN_HALO_WIDTH=Sun Halo Width
option.SUN_HALO_WIDTH.comment=Angular width of the halo (larger = wider and softer)

option.UW_VOLUMETRIC_FOG=Underwater Volumetric Fog

option.UW_SUN_OCCLUSION=Underwater Sun Halo Occlusion
option.UW_SUN_OCCLUSION.comment=Whether the blurry halo toward the sun in underwater fog disappears when the sun is occluded on screen. If the sun is blocked/behind/off-screen the halo hides, keeping the uniform multi-scatter ambient fog

option.BORDER_FOG=Border Fog
option.BORDER_FOG_FALLOFF=Border Fog Falloff

option.GROUND_SCATTERING=Ground Atmospheric Scattering (Aerial Perspective)
option.GROUND_SCATTERING.comment=Separate layer that fades distant terrain toward the atmospheric scattering colour. Decoupled from volumetric fog: no noise, and it does not vanish at noon from "Time Fade". Distant terrain turns blue by day and warm toward the sun. Overworld ground/water only: the sky uses the sky model, the Nether/End keep their own dimension fog; caves and interiors keep a 20% floor (same gate as volumetric fog)
option.GS_DENSITY=Scattering Density
option.GS_DENSITY.comment=Overall density knob (equivalent to scaling the whole ground air path). 0 disables it; higher = hazier distance
option.GS_SUN_BRIGHTNESS=Sun Scattering Brightness
option.GS_SUN_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Mie forward scattering brightness: the warm haze toward the sun. 0 removes the sun-side glow
option.GS_SKY_BRIGHTNESS=Sky Scattering Brightness
option.GS_SKY_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Isotropic sky scattering brightness: the bluish base haze over the distance (day/night tint comes from the sky light itself)
option.GS_MIE_G=Forward Scattering Anisotropy
option.GS_MIE_G.comment=Aerosol phase g: higher concentrates scattering toward the sun (low = spread evenly, high = a bright blob toward the sun)
option.GS_RAIN_BOOST=Rain Density Boost
option.GS_RAIN_BOOST.comment=Extra density multiplier while raining (follows wetness), for the visibility drop in rain. 0 = no rain boost

