option.DEBUG_SKY_MAP=DEBUG_SKY_MAP
option.DEBUG_VOXEL_GI=DEBUG_VOXEL_GI
option.OFFLINE_RENDER=Offline Render
option.OFFLINE_RENDER.comment=Offline render: raise per-pixel diffuse tracing & IRC samples per frame (SPP 20/8), disable GI spatial denoise and keep accumulating temporally for fast convergence to low noise. Hold the camera still (don't orbit) for a while, then F2 for a clean still. Heavy cost; for screenshots. Off = real-time denoise, identical to before
option.VOXEL_COARSE_ACCEL=Voxel Empty-Space Skip
option.VOXEL_COARSE_ACCEL.comment=Skipping tracing DDA over 4^3 coarse blocks that are pure air, avoiding per-voxel fetches. On boosts performance; disable if light leaks / inconsistent lighting appear
option.VOXEL_FINE_ACCEL=Fine-Grain Air Skip
option.VOXEL_FINE_ACCEL.comment=Inside a non-empty coarse block, use the fine-grain occupancy bitmap to skip air cells per-voxel (finer than coarse; enabling it alone also includes the 4^3 empty-block jump). The fine bitmap only covers sun-visible voxelized cells; a solid cell that wasn't voxelized but has injected light/emission is treated as air and skipped -> possible light leaks / hollows. If you see hollows, turn this OFF and keep Empty-Space Skip; per-cell then falls back to real sampling
option.VOXEL_GI_FIREFLY_MEDIAN=Denoise Median (Fireflies)
option.VOXEL_GI_FIREFLY_MEDIAN.comment=After the last SVGF spatial pass, applies a 3x3 median on luminance to remove high-frequency isolated spike noise (fireflies). Default on; disable if the image looks over-smoothed / loses detail
option.VOXEL_LD_SAMPLING=Low-Discrepancy Sampling
option.VOXEL_LD_SAMPLING.comment=Replaces pseudo-random sample directions with a Halton(2,3) low-discrepancy sequence, spreading rays more evenly over the hemisphere across frames and reducing clustering, usually lowering flicker/noise floor. Default off; disable if regular banding/grid artifacts appear
option.VOXEL_COS_SAMPLING=Cosine-Weighted Sampling
option.VOXEL_COS_SAMPLING.comment=Switches to cosine-density sampling (Malley map, pdf∝cosθ) instead of uniform hemisphere x 2cos weight. Same expectation, lower variance: cleaner at equal sampling cost or cheaper at equal noise. Default off; disable & report if indoor/ambient brightness shifts off
option.VOXEL_REUSE=ReSTIR Temporal Reuse
option.VOXEL_REUSE.comment=While the camera is still, re-trace a diffuse sample only every N frames and reuse the previous-frame reservoir in between, saving trace bandwidth. Improves performance and convergence when still/slow-moving; compatible with VOXY builds, only active when the camera is still (motion falls back to per-frame tracing)
option.VOXEL_REUSE_INTERVAL=Re-trace Interval (frames)
option.VOXEL_REUSE_INTERVAL.comment=Re-trace a real sample every N frames (reuse the reservoir mean for the other N-1). Smaller = cleaner still GI but saves less; larger = more frames saved but higher still noise floor. 2-8 is a good gameplay balance
option.VOXEL_REUSE_MCAP=Mean Convergence Cap
option.VOXEL_REUSE_MCAP.comment=Sample-count cap of the reservoir mean accumulation. Larger = lower still noise floor (variance = 1/sqrt(M)) but takes longer to reach; 64 for gameplay, up to 128/256 for screenshots
option.VOXEL_REUSE_THRESHOLD=Full-Speed Convergence Threshold
option.VOXEL_REUSE_THRESHOLD.comment=Until the sample count reaches this value at the start of a static view, re-trace every frame for fast convergence, then switch to sparse reuse. Larger = cleaner still but saves frames later; 16 is a balance
option.DEBUG_VOXEL_SKY=Sky Path Debug
option.DEBUG_VOXEL_SKY.comment=Tints surfaces red where the sky light path is hit, to tell apart "path not reached" vs "value too dim to see"
option.DEBUG_VOXEL_SKY_LEVEL=GI Sky Level Debug
option.DEBUG_VOXEL_SKY_LEVEL.comment=Shows the voxel GI sky level on block surfaces as pseudo-color (IRC sky exposure alpha): blue = no sky light (cave/occluded), red = fully open (open shadow)
option.DEBUG_VOXEL_RADIANCE=DEBUG_VOXEL_RADIANCE

option.VOXEL_GI_DENOISE=Voxel GI Denoise
option.VOXEL_GI_DENOISE.comment=Spatio-temporal variance-guided filtering for voxel GI ray tracing. Disable to show raw half-res checkerboard signal (noisy).
option.VOXEL_GI_DENOISE_MODE=Denoise Scheme
option.VOXEL_GI_DENOISE_MODE.comment=0=SVGF (EAWF a-trous spatial x4, reuses temporal accumulation); 1=PTGI style (single median + depth/normal edge, cheaper). Only affects VXGI; SSILVB unaffected
option.PTGI_MEDIAN_RADIUS=Median Radius
option.PTGI_MEDIAN_RADIUS.comment=1=3x3, 2=5x5. Larger = stronger denoise but blurs detail (targets fireflies/single-pixel noise)
option.PTGI_EDGE_STRENGTH=Edge Preserve Strength
option.PTGI_EDGE_STRENGTH.comment=0=median everywhere (strong denoise, bleeds across edges); 1=median only on flat areas, keeps geometry edges. Recommended 1.0
option.PTGI_BLEND_STRENGTH=Median Blend Strength
option.PTGI_BLEND_STRENGTH.comment=Blends median result with the original (1=pure median, 0=original). Lower keeps more detail but noisier
option.VOXEL_MOON_STRENGTH=Moon Bounce Strength
option.VOXEL_MOON_STRENGTH.comment=Directional moonlight bounce in voxel GI at night (vanilla moonlightMult is too small so moon GI was missing). Moon-facing faces brighten, away faces stay dark; pairs with AO for shading. 0=off; higher = stronger moon GI
option.NRD_RADIUS=Filter World Radius
option.NRD_RADIUS.comment=Target world-space blur radius (m) for EAWF hit-distance adaptive step: near steps up, distant narrows, easing near under-filter & far over-blur. Tuning: 0=off (fixed pixel steps, baseline); 0-0.15 conservative/sharp; 0.15-0.3 balanced (default 0.25); 0.3-0.5 stronger but may spot-flicker/blur near; >0.5 not advised. Flicker near -> lower; far still blurry -> keep >=0.2. Scales with resolution; tune at your render scale
option.NRD_RELIABILITY=Reliability Convergence Rate
option.NRD_RELIABILITY.comment=Exponential reliability history factor (1-exp(-N*rate), N=accumulated frames). Higher reliability -> stronger edge-preserving sigma; few frames (just appeared / reprojected) -> looser filter for fast convergence. 0=off (original SVGF linear history factor); 0.1-0.3 slow convergence, heavy early blur; 0.5 balanced (default); 1-2 fast convergence, strong edge-preserve early (may under-denoise; pair with lower filter radius). Static/far too blurry -> raise; noisy trails while moving -> lower
option.NRD_DISOCCLUSION=Disocclusion Repair
option.NRD_DISOCCLUSION.comment=Fast convergence for newly exposed / disoccluded regions (screen-edge on camera turn, backgrounds revealed by movement, placed blocks): on unreliable pixels widen the spatial step and relax edge-preserving so reliable neighbors fill them quickly, avoiding blur patches and long trails. 0=off; 0.5 mild; 1.0 balanced (default); 2.0+ stronger fill (slight detail loss). Still blurry/trailing at edges -> raise; repair marks / soft detail -> lower
option.VOXEL_DISTANCE=Voxel Distance
option.VOXEL_DISTANCE.comment=Maximum voxelization coverage radius (far cascade); near/mid cascades, distant spherical-harmonic boundary and ray-tracing distance follow proportionally. Requires shadow map resolution >= 1536 (fixed 3-cascade tile height, independent of this distance); below that the far cascade is clipped and effective GI distance drops to half. Keep <= shadow render distance.
option.VOXEL_GI_BLENDED_LIGHTMAP=Blended Lightmap
option.VOXEL_GI_BLENDED_LIGHTMAP.comment=Blend between vanilla lightmap and voxel GI (1.0 = keep vanilla lighting, 0.0 = mask vanilla lightmap, indirect light comes from voxel GI only)

option.VOXEL_GI_STRENGTH=GI Strength
option.VOXEL_GI_STRENGTH.comment=Overall voxel GI brightness multiplier
option.PROBE_GI_ENABLED=Probe Global Illumination
option.PROBE_GI_ENABLED.comment=DDGI-style probe irradiance cache: 16^3 x 4m, smooth low-frequency, denoise-free. Mutually exclusive with voxel/screen-space GI (enable only one); requires ENABLE_VOXELIZATION
option.PROBE_GI_STRENGTH=Probe GI Strength
option.PROBE_GI_STRENGTH.comment=Overall probe indirect-light brightness multiplier
option.PROBE_RAY_SAMPLES=Rays per Probe (per-frame budget)
option.PROBE_RAY_SAMPLES.comment=Average rays cast per probe per frame (total rays/frame = probes x budget, independent of period). Higher = steadier but slower.
option.PROBE_UPDATE_PERIOD=Probe Update Period (frames)
option.PROBE_UPDATE_PERIOD.comment=Each probe updates once every N frames (round-robin); each update casts N x budget rays, lowering per-update variance. N=1 updates every probe every frame (old behavior).
option.PROBE_MAX_FRAMES=Temporal Convergence
option.PROBE_MAX_FRAMES.comment=EMA time constant; lower converges faster but noisier
option.DEBUG_PROBE_PLUMBING=Probe Pipeline Debug
option.DEBUG_PROBE_PLUMBING.comment=Writes a known gradient pattern instead of lighting: full-screen world-anchored gradient = pipeline OK; one corner only = dispatch size wrong; follows camera = query coords wrong; flickering = ping-pong parity wrong

option.VOXEL_GI_TRACE_STRENGTH=Trace GI Strength
option.VOXEL_GI_TRACE_STRENGTH.comment=Overall strength knob for the per-pixel diffuse trace signal; lower if too bright, raise if too dark (cave leak protection is handled by the lightmap leak gate)

option.VOXEL_TRACE_SUN_STRENGTH=Sun Bounce Strength
option.VOXEL_TRACE_SUN_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the sun bounce in per-pixel diffuse tracing (light reflected from sunlit surfaces into shadow). Too low = dark shadows, too high = overexposed.

option.VOXEL_GI_SUN_STRENGTH=Sun Inject Strength
option.VOXEL_GI_SUN_STRENGTH.comment=Sun bounce injection strength into the voxel GI (IRC) cache; raise to make warm golden diffuse light appear in shadowed areas
option.VOXEL_GI_BLOCK_STRENGTH=Blocklight Inject Strength
option.VOXEL_GI_BLOCK_STRENGTH.comment=Block light (torch, lava, etc.) injection strength into the voxel GI (IRC) cache; raise to make torches illuminate further

option.VOXEL_TRACE_DISTANCE=Trace Distance
option.VOXEL_TRACE_DISTANCE.comment=Maximum voxel steps for traced rays; larger = sun/block light travels farther (slightly slower)

option.VOXEL_TRACE_SPP=Rays Per Pixel
option.VOXEL_TRACE_SPP.comment=Diffuse trace rays per pixel per frame (SPP) in realtime mode. 1=current (checkerboard half-res + temporal accumulation); higher averages multiple rays per frame, cleaner and faster convergence, cost scales linearly

option.VOXEL_GI_LIGHT_FALLOFF=Light Falloff
option.VOXEL_GI_LIGHT_FALLOFF.comment=Distance attenuation of emissive light; smaller = wider light reach
option.VOXEL_GI_LIGHT_RADIUS=Light Hit Radius
option.VOXEL_GI_LIGHT_RADIUS.comment=Hit radius of the emissive light sphere; raise so distant rays hit more easily - torches illuminate further, but the glow spills into adjacent voxels

option.VOXEL_GI_SKY_STRENGTH=Sky Inject Strength
option.VOXEL_GI_SKY_STRENGTH.comment=Sky light injection strength on IRC surface hits; higher = more visible outdoor sky GI

option.VOXEL_GI_TRACE_SKY_STRENGTH=Trace Sky Strength
option.VOXEL_GI_TRACE_SKY_STRENGTH.comment=Directional sky strength when traced rays exit the voxel grid

option.VOXEL_TRACE_SKY_GATE=Trace Sky Gate
option.VOXEL_TRACE_SKY_GATE.comment=0=Exit-only: any exiting ray gets directional sky, ignoring vanilla lightmap; 1=Exit+vanilla: lightmap leak gate attenuates caves/semi-occlusion
value.VOXEL_TRACE_SKY_GATE.0=Exit Only
value.VOXEL_TRACE_SKY_GATE.1=Exit + Vanilla
option.VOXEL_IRC_SKY_GATE=IRC Sky Gate
option.VOXEL_IRC_SKY_GATE.comment=0=Existing gate: voxel skylight visibility, suppressed by residual writes in enclosed spaces; 1=Exit-only: full strength on exit, ignores hitSkylight
value.VOXEL_IRC_SKY_GATE.0=Existing Gate
value.VOXEL_IRC_SKY_GATE.1=Exit Only

option.VOXEL_GI_SH_MIX=In-Grid SH Ambient
option.VOXEL_GI_SH_MIX.comment=Restore SH spherical-harmonics ambient inside the voxel grid (additive into GI ambient). SH includes lower-hemisphere irradiance so downward faces are no longer pitch black, and follows the day/night cycle automatically. 0=disabled (pure GI); low values (0.1-0.2) add a subtle floor without flattening GI directionality; 1=full SH flat lighting

option.VOXEL_SKY_REFERENCE=Sky Radiance Reference
option.VOXEL_SKY_REFERENCE.comment=Divisor that maps the physical sky radiance map into the 0-1 lighting scale; larger = darker sky GI, smaller = brighter

# ===== VXGI user switches (Lighting -> Global Illumination -> VXGI) =====
option.ENABLE_VOXELIZATION=Voxelization
option.ENABLE_VOXELIZATION.comment=Voxelization toggle: shadow pass writes voxelData (3D texture) directly; off = no voxel GI. Only affects voxelization itself; to inspect voxels use Debug -> Voxel -> Voxel Visualization

option.VOXEL_GI_SELF_BOUNCE=Self-Bounce Strength
option.VOXEL_GI_SELF_BOUNCE.comment=Weight of the previous-frame IRC radiance used as bounce light on ray hits; determines how deep light propagates into shadows/interiors (higher = brighter but flatter). Values >1 over-amplify self-bounce per hop for propagation debugging / deliberate indirect-light boosting; recommended 0.3-0.8 normally

option.VOXEL_GI_BLEND=Temporal Blend Speed
option.VOXEL_GI_BLEND.comment=History weight of the IRC cache at 60 FPS (0.99 = 99% history, 1% new samples). Lower values respond faster but are noisier.

option.VOXEL_IRC_UPDATE_INTERVAL=IRC Inject Interval
option.VOXEL_IRC_UPDATE_INTERVAL.comment=Re-inject IRC rays into each voxel every N frames, reusing cached values in between; trace cost drops to ~1/N. Voxel indirect light changes slowly, so usually no visible difference; 1 = every frame, 2/4 = every 2/4 frames. Fast camera/world motion lags injection by up to N-1 frames

option.VOXEL_EDGE_BLEND_DISTANCE=Grid Edge Blend Distance
option.VOXEL_EDGE_BLEND_DISTANCE.comment=Distance (in voxels) over which outside-grid ambient light blends into the grid: smoothly transitions from "outside SH ambient" to "inside GI" when new blocks enter the 64^3 range, avoiding dark-to-bright pops at the edge. 0 = disabled

# ===== SSILVB/VXGI 补充翻译 =====
option.SSILVB_GI_BRIGHTNESS=GI Ray Brightness
option.SSILVB_HAND_DEPTH_THRESHOLD=GI Hand Culling
option.SSILVB_HAND_DEPTH_THRESHOLD.comment=Prevents your own hand from affecting the GI; leave at default
option.SVGF_QUALITY=SVGF Quality
option.SVGF_BLUR_RADIUS=SVGF Blur Radius
option.VISUALIZE_VOXELS=Voxel Visualization
option.VISUALIZE_VOXELS.comment=Overlays voxel colors on block albedo to inspect the voxelization result
option.VOXEL_GI_EMISSIVE_THRESHOLD=Emissive Threshold
option.VOXEL_GI_EMISSIVE_THRESHOLD.comment=Blocks whose PBR emissive is below this value are not treated as light sources
option.VOXEL_GI_BOOST=Emissive Boost
option.VOXEL_GI_BOOST.comment=Light energy multiplier for emissive voxels
# ===== 2026-09-12: options that had GUI entries but no text =====
option.NOISE_SIZE=Fog Noise Size
option.NOISE_SIZE.comment=Spatial scale of the volumetric fog 3D noise. Smaller = finer detail and more expensive; larger = big soft clumps. Used together with the fog noise toggle
option.SUN_BRIGHTNESS_MULTIPLIER=Sun Brightness Multiplier
option.SUN_BRIGHTNESS_MULTIPLIER.comment=Scales the intensity of direct sunlight overall. Raise for a brighter look, lower if the image blows out
option.BLOOM_NO_DOWNSAMPLE=Bloom Downsample
option.BLOOM_NO_DOWNSAMPLE.comment=Whether bloom is computed at reduced resolution. On is faster but softer, off is sharper and more expensive
option.SSPT_BLENDED_LIGHTMAP=SSPT Blended Lightmap
option.SSPT_BLENDED_LIGHTMAP.comment=Blend factor between the screen-space path tracing result and Minecraft vanilla lightmap. 0 = vanilla lighting only, 1 = SSPT result only
option.SSPT_MAX_ACCUM_FRAMES=SSPT Max Accumulation Frames
option.SSPT_MAX_ACCUM_FRAMES.comment=Upper bound on SSPT temporal accumulation. Higher = cleaner and more stable, but more ghosting during fast motion
option.DEBUG_SHADOW_WARP=Debug: Shadow Warp Field
option.DEBUG_SHADOW_WARP.comment=Visualises the shadow warp field directly, to check continuity and banding. Debug only, keep off
option.DEBUG_SHADOW_WARP_DIFF=Debug: Warp Table vs Analytic
option.DEBUG_SHADOW_WARP_DIFF.comment=Shows the difference between the table-driven warp and the analytic radial warp, to verify the two implementations agree. Debug only
option.DEBUG_CLOUD_NOISE=Debug: Cloud Noise
option.DEBUG_CLOUD_NOISE.comment=Outputs the raw cloud noise texture, for diagnosing malformed clouds. Debug only
option.DEBUG_ATMOSPHERE_LUTS=Debug: Atmosphere LUTs
option.DEBUG_ATMOSPHERE_LUTS.comment=Displays the atmosphere scattering lookup tables (transmittance, multiple scattering, etc.), for diagnosing wrong sky colours. Debug only
option.DEBUG_TONE_MAPPING_PLOT=Debug: Tone Mapping Curve
option.DEBUG_TONE_MAPPING_PLOT.comment=Plots the current tone mapping response curve, for comparing how different mappers roll off highlights. Debug only
# ===== Not wired up: implementation removed, these currently do nothing =====
option.FXAA_ENABLED=FXAA (not wired)
option.FXAA_ENABLED.comment=Note: the FXAA implementation was removed with the dead-code cleanup, so this toggle currently does nothing. To enable it, restore shaders/program/post/FXAA.glsl from git history and wire it up
option.RSM_ENABLED=Enable RSM (not wired)
option.RSM_ENABLED.comment=Reflective Shadow Maps gives one-bounce indirect light. Note: RSM.glsl was never included anywhere and has been removed with the dead-code cleanup, so this toggle currently does nothing. To enable it, restore shaders/lib/lighting/RSM.glsl from git history and first fix its duplicate definition of realShadowMapRes (already defined in settings.glsl)
option.RSM_SAMPLES=RSM Samples (not wired)
option.RSM_SAMPLES.comment=Note: RSM is not wired up (implementation removed); this option currently does nothing
option.RSM_RADIUS=RSM Radius (not wired)
option.RSM_RADIUS.comment=Note: RSM is not wired up (implementation removed); this option currently does nothing
option.RSM_BRIGHTNESS=RSM Brightness (not wired)
option.RSM_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Note: RSM is not wired up (implementation removed); this option currently does nothing
option.RSM_MAX_ACCUM_FRAMES=RSM Max Accumulation Frames (not wired)
option.RSM_MAX_ACCUM_FRAMES.comment=Note: RSM is not wired up (implementation removed); this option currently does nothing
